WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.587
Correct retrieval does not guarantee correct generation.

00:00:03.587 --> 00:00:10.472
Even if the right evidence is present, the model may misread it, omit part of it, cite the wrong source,

00:00:10.472 --> 00:00:14.157
or perform an action it is not authorized to perform.

00:00:14.157 --> 00:00:17.274
That is why generation should also be validated.

00:00:17.724 --> 00:00:22.821
Grounding validation asks whether factual claims are supported by the evidence.

00:00:22.821 --> 00:00:30.296
Citation validation asks whether the cited source I D's actually match supplied evidence.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:35.016
Format validation checks whether required fields are present.

00:00:35.016 --> 00:00:39.961
Business-rule validation checks boundaries that should not depend on the model.

00:00:40.522 --> 00:00:48.078
For example, the model may correctly explain a refund policy but should not automatically issue a refund unless the

00:00:48.078 --> 00:00:51.427
workflow has explicit authorization for that action.
